WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.480
Today we are stepping outside into the Russian skies to master everyday weather words that let you talk about sun, wind and snow like a local.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:20.520
I'm Olya, and this is Привет, Русский, episode 69. Our word of the day is Vetyr. Vetyr. Why ye tea? It means wind.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:28.500
Think of a veteran sailor who knows every gust of wind. Vetyr do it сильно. The wind is blowing strongly.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:36.700
Repeat after me, Vetyr. Now let's build more weather words. Remember pogoda from before, it means weather.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:51.500
Our next word is snick, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk, snk.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:04.560
Repeat after me, snk, snk. Next comes oblok, oblok , oblaka, oblaka. It means cloud, say oblaka like oblaka, it blocks the sun.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:12.180
Bolshoi oblaka pleasant to the sky. Abig cloud is floating across the sky, repeat after me oblaka.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.840
Нау вы move to temporary words.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:15.580
Тепло.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:16.480
Тепло.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.380
It means warm or warms.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.580
Sounds like tapet, but means pleasantly warm.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:23.700
Сегодня тепло на улице.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.520
It is warm outside today.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:26.960
Repeat after me.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:27.540
тепло.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:29.840
The opposite is холодно.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:30.640
холодно.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:31.100
Х.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:31.760
лодна.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.360
It means cold in an impersonal way.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:34.780
Х.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:35.480
лодна.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.380
Imagine a halo of frost around you.

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:40.400
Зимой холодно в сибири.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.820
It is cold in Siberia in winter.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.260
Repeat after me.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:44.960
холодно.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.040
Ахе в рейне is living.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:47.880
Ливень.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:48.740
Ливень.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:50.540
It means downpour.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.740
Ливень, like a living river pouring from the sky.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.680
Ливень идёт весь день.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.940
A downpour is falling all day.

00:01:58.580 --> 00:01:59.360
Repeat after me.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:01:59.920
Ливень.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.240
Обеек сторм из гроза.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:02.960
Гроза.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:03.740
Гроза.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:05.120
It means thunderstorm.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:09.560
Гроза sounds like grace, but brings lightning instead of cows.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.920
Гроза громкая и яркая.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.320
The thunderstorm is loud and bright.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:15.720
Repeat after me.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:16.280
Гроза.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:18.440
Finally, we have temperature.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:19.800
Температура.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:21.640
Температура.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:22.080
Температура.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.760
It means temperature.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.640
Almost the same as English.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:26.960
Just roll the R.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.300
Какая температура на улице?

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.080
Вот это температура outside.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:32.620
Repeat after me.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:33.500
Температура.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.760
Let's look at one simple grammar idea.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:40.660
In Russian we often skip the subject when talking about weather.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.300
We just say тепло.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:43.700
It means it is warm.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.080
Or холодно.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:46.400
It means it is cold.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.200
Сегодня ветрано.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.300
It is windy today.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:53.540
Unlike English, we drop the heat and use the Edward directly.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.640
Now you can say a full weather thought in Russian.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:00.060
There is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:04.000
Vietr started an ancient proto-slavic as Vietr.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.160
It shares a very old route with English wind

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.740
that goes all the way back to the same source, meaning to blow.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:15.280
It travels through centuries of Slavic languages without changing much.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.920
English kept a similar sound but spelt it differently.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:20.160
Be careful.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:23.620
The Russian Vietr sounds nothing like the English veteran,

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.640
even though they share some letters.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.980
Picture a veteran's sailor shouting Vietr,

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.240
every time a gust hits the sails.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:33.760
The Russians love to talk about the weather

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:36.720
because it changes dramatically across their huge country.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.100
From snowy winter since Siberia

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.180
to warm summers near the Black Sea.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.200
People often greet each other with a quick comment

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.820
about the temperature or wind.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.380
It is a friendly way to start conversation.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.380
Now it's practice time.

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:52.940
For kids draw a picture of today's weather.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.340
Label the sun, clouds and wind

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:56.600
with the new Russian words.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:58.960
Then say each word out loud.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:02.000
For adults, look out the window right now.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:05.220
Make one simple sentence in Russian about the weather

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.240
using at least two new words.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.280
And that's our lesson for today.

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.220
Molodezh for sticking with it.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.960
